  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Better inclusion, greater rights: improving the economic integration of disadvantaged groups in the City of Buenos Aires</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">La Asociacin Civil por la Igualdad y la Justicia (ACIJ), $49,950 over one year Through a planning grant, ACIJ will carry out a participatory study to collect information on the principal causes of the lack of access to the formal economy for residents of 10 irregular settlements (Villas) in greater Buenos Aires. The design, collection, and analysis of information will be supervised by ACIJ and jointly carried out with residents of the Villas in order to increase their capacity to identify problems and develop solutions. The study will also identify existing resources, potential public, private and non-profit partners, and formal and informal networks working to build the residents entrepreneurial capacity to succeed in the formal economy. Approximately 60 residents will benefit directly.</narrative>
  </description>
